# Build output - always regenerable with `dotnet build`, never worth tracking. This is also
# where WebView2 parks its own runtime user-data profile (cache, cookies, local storage) next
# to the built exe, so ignoring bin/ catches that too.
[Bb]in/
[Oo]bj/

# Visual Studio / Rider local-only project state
.vs/
.idea/
*.user
*.suo

# MSFS toolbar panel (see msfs-toolbar-panel/) - build.bat's own output, not source. The
# top-level Build/ it assembles is the final package folder ready to copy into Community; the
# Packages/_Temp subfolders are fspackagetool's own intermediates, created inside
# realefb-ingamepanel/Build/ alongside the PackageDefinitions/PackageSources XML that IS
# source (hence the narrower patterns below rather than ignoring every Build/ folder outright).
# The compiled .spb itself is a binary regenerated by every build - never worth tracking either.
/msfs-toolbar-panel/Build/
msfs-toolbar-panel/**/Build/Packages/
msfs-toolbar-panel/**/Build/_Temp/
msfs-toolbar-panel/**/InGamePanels/*.spb

# OS cruft
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
